---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Explainers"
  description="Short, plain-English explanations of the concepts behind onshore investing in China: capital accounts, the USD 50,000 quota, NRA accounts and qualified investors."
>
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">Concepts</p>
    <h1 style="margin-top:.6rem">Explainers</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A handful of ideas explain most of the confusion about investing in China. Each one is short,
      and each one changes what you are allowed to do.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <a class="card card--link" href="/explainers/capital-vs-current-account">
        <span class="card__kicker">The big one</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.22rem">Current account vs capital account</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          Why salary money can cross the border and investment money cannot, and why a completed
          transfer is not proof of legality.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/explainers/usd-50k-quota">
        <span class="card__kicker">Misunderstood</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.22rem">The USD 50,000 quota</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          A conversion quota for current-account purposes — not an investment allowance. What it
          covers, and what splitting it costs you.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/explainers/nra-account">
        <span class="card__kicker">Account types</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.22rem">What an NRA account is</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          An onshore account for non-residents. Useful for payments, not a licence to invest.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/explainers/qualified-investor">
        <span class="card__kicker">Thresholds</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.22rem">Who counts as a qualified investor</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          The CNY 3 million / CNY 500,000 test that gates private funds, and why most residents never
          meet it.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/explainers/tax-residency-183-days">
        <span class="card__kicker">The one that decides the rest</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.22rem">The 183-day rule</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          How China decides you are a tax resident, the six-year rule behind it, and why your visa
          type does not settle the question.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/explainers/withholding-tax">
        <span class="card__kicker">Why the number is smaller</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.22rem">Withholding on dividends and interest</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          What is deducted before the money reaches you, why residents and non-residents differ, and
          what to keep for your home-country return.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/explainers/deposit-insurance">
        <span class="card__kicker">The ceiling nobody mentions</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.22rem">Deposit insurance: CNY 500,000</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          The protection ceiling per depositor per bank, what counts as a deposit, and why “wealth
          management” is not one.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/explainers/risk-grades">
        <span class="card__kicker">The gate you did not choose</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.22rem">Risk grades R1 to R5</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          Product grades and your tolerance grade have to match, and for many foreign residents the
          second one is set lower than their experience.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/explainers/fund-share-classes">
        <span class="card__kicker">Two classes, one question</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.22rem">A-class and C-class fund shares</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          Front load versus trailing fee. The breakeven is a division you can do yourself, and it is
          usually shorter than the salesperson implies.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/explainers/treaty-relief">
        <span class="card__kicker">A piece of paper</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.22rem">Claiming a treaty rate</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          The difference between 5% and 10% withholding is a certificate from your home tax office.
          What it is, who issues it, and why silence costs you.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/explainers/equity-compensation">
        <span class="card__kicker">Three taxable moments</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.22rem">When employee equity is taxed</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          Grant, vest, sale. The employer withholds on the second before you can act, and the third
          depends on where you are tax resident.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="card card--link" href="/glossary">
        <span class="card__kicker">Reference</span>
        <h2 class="card__title" style="font-size:1.22rem">Glossary of the words on the form</h2>
        <p class="card__body">
          Fifty-five terms, with pinyin, that decide what happens at the counter — from 面签 to 完税证明.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
